  "stage": {
    "routeId": "camino-frances",
    "index": 15,
    "count": 33,
    "name": "Frómista to Carrión de los Condes",
    "theme": "Surrender",
    "narrative": "You did not quit. And in the wake of that survival, an easy, flat day, and in that ease something softens. The Romanesque church of San Martín in Frómista is considered one of the most perfect in Spain — symmetrical, proportioned, complete. You do not need to understand architecture to feel what it offers: the peace of something made with total devotion and no hurry. Carrión de los Condes was once a major medieval city. Now it is a quiet town that knows how to receive tired walkers. You are learning to receive, too.",
    "closing": "What would happen if you stopped trying to earn your rest?",
